    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0445" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2389a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-07T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 7, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Please report in detail as to operations of British submarines in the Baltic,
                    including the kind of warning given to merchant vessels, the care taken of
                    passengers and crew, whether visit and search was carried out, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
